  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Issue\n\nAn ongoing issue with a world in-development has been occurring; details are as follows:\n\n- The first person to spawn into a room is owner\n\n- The owner can interact with Udon objects, as per normal\n\n- **Subsequent players who join in receive references to instances of the objects per normal**; This is confirmed via logging.\n\n- *However*, **attempting to read properties from these objects crashes the udon behavior, with the error** \"*Object reference not set to an instance of an object.*\"\n\n- To reiterate, this does not happen to the first to join; **only subsequent joiners.** — *This includes the first to join* **if they initiate \"rejoin world\" at any point, or leave the world at any time.**\n\n \n\n# Environment(s)\n\n**Tested Clients:**\n\n- PC (Live, Latest)\n\n- Quest (Live, Beta 1220, 1222)\n\n \n\nSDKs:\n\n- Live (Latest)\n\n- Live (Latest, VPM)\n\n- Beta (3.1.6-Beta 1, VPM)\n\n \n\n# Logs & Information\n\n- Relevant Logs: [HomeOffice.log](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/657394772603830360/1009071617546145842/HomeOffice.log)\n\n \n\n# Relevant Programs\n\n- [Udon Program Assets (Archive)](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/657394772603830360/1009071617869090926/Udon_Program_Assets.zip)\n\n \n\n# Additional Notes\n\n- Relevant objects are public variables assigned via the inspector.\n\n- As variables do return valid instances for first player, this is unspecified/unexpected behavior.\n\n- Udon programs have gone through numerous iterations and complete rewrites in attempts to solve issues. Current programs attached are not the only effected, in essence; seemingly effects all synced udon programs in-world.",
